:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186390688}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "8a41594a-f79c-59b8-b328-4364bfa01e24" :question/math-academy-id "q-317898" :question/problem "Which of the following is the graph of  $y=-{(\\frac{3}{10})}^{x+1}?$" :question/worked-solution "To plot the given function, we follow these steps:\n\n- We take the curve $y={(\\frac{3}{10})}^{x}.$\n\n![](images/a9/a9b6c2b12c1bc4bc7794dd5d409a99c61bf256ea58f9a016657cbbea5ef6b1e4.png)\n\n \n\n- Horizontally shift it by $1$ units to the left to give $y={(\\frac{3}{10})}^{x+1}.$ The $y$-intercept moves from $(0,1)$ to $(-1,1)$ but the horizontal asymptote stays at $y=0.$\n\n![](images/5f/5f4c0e3c4573f6e3167390d54ee21bbb8bf6e3879fcc06e7adf9d311e80ccb62.png)\n\n- Then, reflect it on the $x$-axis to give $y=-{(\\frac{3}{10})}^{x+1}.$ The point $(-1,1)$ moves to $(-1,-1)$ and the horizontal asymptote stays at $y=0.$\n\n![](images/b5/b541282b8661f2fb28d0ce1f10c22a9a8cc7b083460c05093a89722bc084d7b9.png)"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186299772 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186115401 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "4c1def23-83e0-5dc7-b20b-9693127d3a9e" :knowledge-point/title "Differentiating Inverse Reciprocal Trigonometric Functions Using the Chain Rule"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "01348264-a81e-56c3-895f-616259a8e027" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{6}{|6x-1|\\sqrt{9{x}^{2}-3x}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186297556} {:answer/id #uuid "0394f679-9a1c-5b87-94ed-5055b0ccff99" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{6}{|6x-1|\\sqrt{9{x}^{2}-3x}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186297572} {:answer/id #uuid "50c36e45-828c-545f-9d7e-4d60c934349c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{6}{|6x-1|\\sqrt{3{x}^{2}-x}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186297888} {:answer/id #uuid "5a70b39e-a686-576d-b119-facfb9478e8f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{1}{|6x-1|\\sqrt{3{x}^{2}-x}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186297932} {:answer/id #uuid "fe851005-bb92-50a4-8f77-18e97f095b87" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{|6x-1|\\sqrt{9{x}^{2}-3x}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186298643}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "0394f679-9a1c-5b87-94ed-5055b0ccff99" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{6}{|6x-1|\\sqrt{9{x}^{2}-3x}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186297572} :answer-field/id #uuid "29c39276-107a-53e2-88ed-bb72cf785946" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186298779}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "1b0ce731-e82d-557a-b699-13d5ea673ea4" :question/math-academy-id "q-31951" :question/problem "Find ${f}^{′}(x)$ if $f(x)=2arcsec(6x-1).$" :question/worked-solution "The formula for the derivative of $arcsec$ is\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(arcsecx)=\\frac{1}{|x|\\sqrt{{x}^{2}-1}}.\n$$\n\nUsing the chain rule and the formula above, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{′}(x) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(2arcsec(6x-1)) \\\\  & =2\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(arcsec(6x-1)) \\\\  & =2\\cdot \\frac{1}{|6x-1|\\sqrt{(6x-1)^{2}-1}}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(6x-1) \\\\  & =2\\cdot \\frac{1}{|6x-1|\\sqrt{{(6x-1)}^{2}-1}}\\cdot 6 \\\\  & =\\frac{12}{|6x-1|\\sqrt{36{x}^{2}-12x}} \\\\  & =\\frac{12}{|6x-1|\\sqrt{4(9{x}^{2}-3x)}} \\\\  & =\\frac{6}{|6x-1|\\sqrt{9{x}^{2}-3x}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186299806 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186078459 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "fb183013-a42d-50a3-a1b8-cd8501781075" :knowledge-point/title "Factoring a Polynomial With Multiple Variables as a Difference of Squares"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "17f420e0-2ce0-5aca-8dee-2fc02f4be838" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "({x}^{2}+{y}^{3})({x}^{2}-{y}^{3})" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186297656} {:answer/id #uuid "2decc769-5d34-52a4-8f61-0d917cf2c0e6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "({x}^{5}+{y}^{2})(x-{y}^{4})" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186297746} {:answer/id #uuid "84d3cf7b-8bb1-5c05-bad0-4556bf860b32" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "({x}^{3}+{y}^{3})({x}^{2}-{y}^{2})" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186298125} {:answer/id #uuid "903c4fc8-2bfb-5749-a8dc-9a4f1681fb2d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "({x}^{3}+{y}^{2})({x}^{3}-{y}^{2})" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186298178} {:answer/id #uuid "bd0ab2a9-e83d-55df-8e55-44c8b207e2a8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "({x}^{2}+{y}^{2})({x}^{2}-{y}^{2})" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186298375}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "17f420e0-2ce0-5aca-8dee-2fc02f4be838" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "({x}^{2}+{y}^{3})({x}^{2}-{y}^{3})" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186297656} :answer-field/id #uuid "710ade4f-6788-57df-bfae-27eab8eaa863" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186299022}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "a03ef93a-a766-5bc2-9cd5-d8ee9f70bca4" :question/math-academy-id "q-31991" :question/problem "Factor ${x}^{4}-{y}^{6}.$" :question/worked-solution "The difference of squares formula is given by\n\n$$\n{a}^{2}-{b}^{2}=(a+b)(a-b)\n$$\n\nNotice that our expression can be written as a difference of squares:\n\n$$\n{x}^{4}-{y}^{6}={({x}^{2})}^{2}-{({y}^{3})}^{2}\n$$\n\nFinally, we factor our expression using the difference of squares formula:\n\n$$\n{({x}^{2})}^{2}-{({y}^{3})}^{2}=({x}^{2}+{y}^{3})({x}^{2}-{y}^{3})\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186115739 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186115401 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "4c1def23-83e0-5dc7-b20b-9693127d3a9e" :knowledge-point/title "Differentiating Inverse Reciprocal Trigonometric Functions Using the Chain Rule"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "006c4d37-009e-5065-aa0e-e789bc12caf9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{4{x}^{3}}{|8-{x}^{4}|\\sqrt{(8-{x}^{4})^{2}-1}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186297551} {:answer/id #uuid "a3a34a37-aaa2-5b33-8413-e4f969d084a1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{12{x}^{3}}{|8-{x}^{4}|\\sqrt{(8-{x}^{4})^{2}-1}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186298270} {:answer/id #uuid "bb221971-81aa-5b2d-a077-c6b670f32b1b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{8{x}^{3}}{|8-{x}^{4}|\\sqrt{(8-{x}^{4})^{2}-1}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186298367} {:answer/id #uuid "c0e98b1b-1585-5bcb-a6c7-f9e80aef1351" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{6{x}^{3}}{|8-{x}^{4}|\\sqrt{(8-{x}^{4})^{2}-1}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186298401} {:answer/id #uuid "cd44316a-87ed-548b-af75-38a85154bbc0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{12{x}^{3}}{|8-{x}^{4}|\\sqrt{(8-{x}^{4})^{2}-1}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186298447}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "bb221971-81aa-5b2d-a077-c6b670f32b1b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{8{x}^{3}}{|8-{x}^{4}|\\sqrt{(8-{x}^{4})^{2}-1}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186298367} :answer-field/id #uuid "b39d87eb-5482-5669-84b6-1f25fa680a00" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186299244}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "c5f8a50f-d033-5259-86d9-bade982764d7" :question/math-academy-id "q-32000" :question/problem "Calculate ${f}^{′}(x)$ for $f(x)=2arccsc(8-{x}^{4}).$" :question/worked-solution "The formula for the derivative of $\\text{arccsc}$ is\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(\\text{arccsc}\\,x)=-\\frac{1}{|x|\\sqrt{{x}^{2}-1}}.\n$$\n\nUsing the chain rule and the formula above, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{′}(x) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(2arccsc(8-{x}^{4})) \\\\  & =2\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(arccsc(8-{x}^{4})) \\\\  & =2(-\\frac{1}{|8-{x}^{4}|\\sqrt{(8-{x}^{4})^{2}-1}})\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(8-{x}^{4}) \\\\  & =2(-\\frac{1}{|8-{x}^{4}|\\sqrt{(8-{x}^{4})^{2}-1}})\\cdot (-4{x}^{3}) \\\\  & =\\frac{8{x}^{3}}{|8-{x}^{4}|\\sqrt{(8-{x}^{4})^{2}-1}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186390711 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186092183 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "c89778fa-3c8d-5f0a-a0f8-c9b3d9193ffd" :knowledge-point/title "Solving a 2x2 System of Equations Using an Inverse Matrix"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "b2cf0dd5-0db7-57a2-9870-1611db6da665" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x=\\frac{1}{5}[\\begin{aligned}3 & -1 \\\\ 2 & 1\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186390713} {:answer/id #uuid "be6ce68f-4c42-58da-863b-b22d6376ce30" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x=[\\begin{aligned}-3 & -1 \\\\ 2 & -1\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186390714} {:answer/id #uuid "333a570b-447e-5d5d-9439-65c7fcbb64c1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x=-\\frac{1}{5}[\\begin{aligned}3 & -1 \\\\ 2 & 1\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186390715} {:answer/id #uuid "ae5e534f-499c-5a4d-9bd0-1ecbfeee8157" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x=\\frac{1}{5}[\\begin{aligned}3 & 1 \\\\ -2 & 1\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186390716} {:answer/id #uuid "f518abcf-bf8c-56aa-bf15-d5e00e0d770d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 \\\\ -2 & 3\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186390717}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "ae5e534f-499c-5a4d-9bd0-1ecbfeee8157" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x=\\frac{1}{5}[\\begin{aligned}3 & 1 \\\\ -2 & 1\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186390716} :answer-field/id #uuid "89bea882-0921-5708-a9f9-9d676afb881e" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186390712}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "ffd8425a-ff52-5722-b741-7d19394751e5" :question/math-academy-id "q-32136" :question/problem "Which of the following represents the solution to the system of linear equations given below?\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}x-y=-1 \\\\ 2x+3y=0\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/worked-solution "This system can be written as\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}1 & -1 \\\\ 2 & 3\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nTo find the solution, we need to calculate the inverse of the coefficient matrix \n$A=[\\begin{aligned}1 & -1 \\\\ 2 & 3\\end{aligned}].$\nThis gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{A}^{-1} & =\\frac{1}{1\\cdot 3-(-1)\\cdot 2}[\\begin{aligned}3 & 1 \\\\ -2 & 1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{5}[\\begin{aligned}3 & 1 \\\\ -2 & 1\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe can now represent the solution to this system, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x & ={A}^{-1}b \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{5}[\\begin{aligned}3 & 1 \\\\ -2 & 1\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186390718 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186092183 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "c89778fa-3c8d-5f0a-a0f8-c9b3d9193ffd" :knowledge-point/title "Solving a 2x2 System of Equations Using an Inverse Matrix"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "af53f340-3e36-5545-937e-11e307962671" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x=-\\frac{1}{50}[\\begin{aligned}2 & -6 \\\\ -8 & 1\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}46 \\\\ -23\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186390720} {:answer/id #uuid "f3ec4ea9-2509-5c2c-a216-2db5287d79fb" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x=-\\frac{1}{46}[\\begin{aligned}1 & -8 \\\\ -6 & 2\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}46 \\\\ -23\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186390721} {:answer/id #uuid "99392c81-e8f0-5fb5-ae4c-99f2a069feb9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x=\\frac{1}{50}[\\begin{aligned}1 & 6 \\\\ 8 & 2\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}46 \\\\ -23\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186390722} {:answer/id #uuid "bff6331c-295a-540c-a6d8-28d96895301d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x=\\frac{1}{46}[\\begin{aligned}2 & 6 \\\\ 8 & 1\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}46 \\\\ -23\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186390723} {:answer/id #uuid "4d16e9a1-1407-53d0-b940-8956dc7a7aa2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x=-\\frac{1}{46}[\\begin{aligned}1 & -6 \\\\ -8 & 2\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}46 \\\\ -23\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186390724}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "4d16e9a1-1407-53d0-b940-8956dc7a7aa2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x=-\\frac{1}{46}[\\begin{aligned}1 & -6 \\\\ -8 & 2\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}46 \\\\ -23\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186390724} :answer-field/id #uuid "94a86967-5a41-5f2d-8c19-38b625daba3c" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186390719}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "34c426c5-7657-5020-93fd-26e20c441212" :question/math-academy-id "q-32139" :question/problem "Which of the following represents the solution to the system of linear equations given below?\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}2x+6y=46 \\\\ 8x+y=-23\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/worked-solution "This system can be written as\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}2 & 6 \\\\ 8 & 1\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}46 \\\\ -23\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nTo find the solution, we need to calculate the inverse of the coefficient matrix \n$A=[\\begin{aligned}2 & 6 \\\\ 8 & 1\\end{aligned}].$\nThis gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{A}^{-1} & =\\frac{1}{2\\cdot 1-6\\cdot 8}[\\begin{aligned}1 & -6 \\\\ -8 & 2\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{46}[\\begin{aligned}1 & -6 \\\\ -8 & 2\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe can now represent the solution to this system, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x & ={A}^{-1}b \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{46}[\\begin{aligned}1 & -6 \\\\ -8 & 2\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}46 \\\\ -23\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186120195 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186119940 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "0305491f-5ac7-5ba4-9a80-1a9a79b964f0" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating dy/dx at a Point Using dx/dy"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2104e133-914f-5ccf-9abb-bb338526ec6d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{7}{18}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186300116} {:answer/id #uuid "2e7b2fae-8ac3-57a0-bffe-05751f19e1e4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{54}{7}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186300187} {:answer/id #uuid "9e343b3d-6257-5d65-9a7e-1c0b02359997" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{9}{5}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186300760} {:answer/id #uuid "a782896a-abec-59e4-9290-6a432fe3815a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{5}{9}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186300805} {:answer/id #uuid "bebe977a-dc05-5a44-8579-fd4c6afc897a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{18}{7}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186300914}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "bebe977a-dc05-5a44-8579-fd4c6afc897a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{18}{7}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186300914} :answer-field/id #uuid "38691da1-c3cd-5bcd-bc71-b36d06760bd6" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186301409}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "e944b722-89ed-5df5-8b31-cb3570eaaf1f" :question/math-academy-id "q-32595" :question/problem "If $x=2\\sqrt{y}-\\frac{3}{\\sqrt{y}},$ find $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}$ at the point $(5,9).$" :question/worked-solution "First, we differentiate $x(y)$ with respect to $y:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}y} & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}y}(2\\sqrt{y}-\\frac{3}{\\sqrt{y}}) \\\\  & =2\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}y}(\\sqrt{y})-3\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}y}(\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{y}}) \\\\  & =2\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}y}({y}^{1/2})-3\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}y}({y}^{-1/2}) \\\\  & =2\\cdot \\frac{1}{2}{y}^{-1/2}-3\\cdot (-\\frac{1}{2}{y}^{-3/2}) \\\\  & ={y}^{-1/2}+\\frac{3}{2}{y}^{-3/2} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{y}}+\\frac{3}{2\\sqrt{{y}^{3}}} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{y}}+\\frac{3}{2y\\sqrt{y}} \\\\  & =\\frac{2y+3}{2y\\sqrt{y}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, taking the reciprocal of $\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}y},$ we get\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}={(\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}y})}^{-1}=\\frac{2y\\sqrt{y}}{2y+3}.\n$$\n\nFinally, substituting the point $(5,9),$ we find\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}{|}_{(x,y)=(5,9)} & =\\frac{2(9)\\sqrt{9}}{2(9)+3}=\\frac{18}{7}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186120196 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186119941 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "4ff302ba-5a3f-599b-b038-7417af1dca71" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Equation of a Tangent Line Using dx/dy"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "16d73b7d-9403-55ab-b551-e19830698e26" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=\\frac{x}{12}+\\frac{9}{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186300052} {:answer/id #uuid "6a33eeae-06c8-52d2-b05c-f45a9e998a06" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=\\frac{x}{12}+\\frac{7}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186300498} {:answer/id #uuid "9e0ef0fa-a60f-528b-b723-df752ee1c670" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=\\frac{x}{12}+\\frac{7}{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186300758} {:answer/id #uuid "b2d76d1c-be51-51c6-8cde-9ba71e9a668a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=9x+3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186300855} {:answer/id #uuid "b6e2c41b-b138-5e44-b020-de7bc94b2004" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=12x-27" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186300874}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "16d73b7d-9403-55ab-b551-e19830698e26" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=\\frac{x}{12}+\\frac{9}{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186300052} :answer-field/id #uuid "2a3602d1-8784-558b-8e8c-d79f5c14e514" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186301360}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "c7ef2446-7ddb-53cb-83cf-b4fed6b4ea6f" :question/math-academy-id "q-32596" :question/problem "Given a curve $x=\\frac{2}{3}{y}^{3}-{y}^{2},$ what is the equation of the tangent to the curve at the point $(9,3)?$" :question/worked-solution "First, we differentiate $x(y)$ with respect to $y:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}y} & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}y}(\\frac{2}{3}{y}^{3}-{y}^{2}) \\\\  & =\\frac{2}{3}\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}y}({y}^{3})-\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}y}({y}^{2}) \\\\  & =\\frac{2}{3}\\cdot 3{y}^{2}-2y \\\\  & =2{y}^{2}-2y\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, taking the reciprocal of $\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}y},$ we get\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}={(\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}y})}^{-1}=\\frac{1}{2{y}^{2}-2y}.\n$$\n\nThe slope of the tangent to the curve at the point $(9,3)$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}m & =\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}{|}_{(x,y)=(9,3)} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2(3)^{2}-2(3)} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{12}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nUsing the point-slope formula for a tangent line, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y-{y}_{1} & =m(x-{x}_{1}) \\\\ y-3 & =\\frac{1}{12}(x-9) \\\\ y & =\\frac{x}{12}-\\frac{3}{4}+3 \\\\ y & =\\frac{x}{12}+\\frac{9}{4}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186120198 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186119978 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "8c0b7d95-c699-5762-aa44-449712f035c7" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating the Derivative of the Inverse of a Polynomial Function"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "319c0fb3-aee5-5e2d-bcbf-a1949dbc941d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{2{g}^{-1}(x)+6}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186300206} {:answer/id #uuid "896ccbe6-a82d-5b23-9d7c-b0f373d22b40" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4{g}^{-1}(x)+6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186300656} {:answer/id #uuid "da6d18f3-3cee-525c-86e4-e352d45bb12f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{1}{4{g}^{-1}(x)+6}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186301044} {:answer/id #uuid "f2c1668d-0e47-5c9f-bcd8-84e9ad090306" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{4{g}^{-1}(x)+6}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186301161} {:answer/id #uuid "ff0f86e0-2705-5cc9-b536-c3f797b75455" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{2({g}^{-1}(x))+6{g}^{-1}(x)-2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186301223}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "f2c1668d-0e47-5c9f-bcd8-84e9ad090306" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{4{g}^{-1}(x)+6}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186301161} :answer-field/id #uuid "348b05f8-ac66-5d57-a5c3-05e956512cbf" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186301392}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "62e6ddbb-e71d-53d4-9a83-95cdcae2804b" :question/math-academy-id "q-32629" :question/problem "If $g(x)=2{x}^{2}+6x-2,$ find ${({g}^{-1})}^{′}(x)$ as a function of ${g}^{-1}(x).$" :question/worked-solution "**Step 1:** First, we write the inverse function implicitly. The given function is $y=2{x}^{2}+6x-2,$ and to write the inverse function implicitly, we swap $x$ and $y$ as follows:\n\n$$\nx=2{y}^{2}+6y-2\n$$\n\nNote that in the equation above, we have $y={g}^{-1}(x).$\n\n**Step 2:** Next, we differentiate. The overall goal is to find $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x},$ but the equation is already solved for $x,$ so we compute $\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}y}$ and then take the reciprocal:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}y} & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}y}(2{y}^{2}+6y-2) \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}y} & =4y+6 \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =\\frac{1}{4y+6}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n**Step 3:**\n\nLastly, we write the result in terms of ${g}^{-1}(x).$ Since $y={g}^{-1}(x),$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}[{g}^{-1}(x)] & =\\frac{1}{4{g}^{-1}(x)+6} \\\\ {({g}^{-1})}^{′}(x) & =\\frac{1}{4{g}^{-1}(x)+6}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186302290 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186119979 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "0196af83-9ef6-5bab-9f50-0aacf488f0cc" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating the Derivative of the Inverse of a Composite Function"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2e68e0e6-041a-534e-ae3f-656e3055c656" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{2}\\,\\operatorname{csc}⁡(2{g}^{-1}(x)+5)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186300186} {:answer/id #uuid "3d41be64-6ef0-5cb2-8c49-dfdb88df1918" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{2}\\,\\operatorname{sec}⁡(2{g}^{-1}(x)+5)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186300260} {:answer/id #uuid "3ed454bc-d138-582d-9b57-ad9bfb532c15" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2\\operatorname{csc}⁡(2{g}^{-1}(x)+5)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186300270} {:answer/id #uuid "77e1d8bb-f34a-54b5-88c5-760321bf0433" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2{g}^{-1}(x)+5)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186300552} {:answer/id #uuid "7f545b1d-f3a2-5eae-aa1d-a60253aadbbe" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\operatorname{sec}⁡(2{g}^{-1}(x))" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186300594}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "3d41be64-6ef0-5cb2-8c49-dfdb88df1918" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{2}\\,\\operatorname{sec}⁡(2{g}^{-1}(x)+5)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186300260} :answer-field/id #uuid "f6625e80-6f3e-5f94-979a-72f6d57fbe39" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186302013}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "2318ec9c-3e92-5221-b4ff-d2d8a492f82d" :question/math-academy-id "q-32635" :question/problem "If $g(x)=\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2x+5)-1,$ find ${({g}^{-1})}^{′}(x)$ as a function of ${g}^{-1}(x).$" :question/worked-solution "**Step 1:** First, we write the inverse function implicitly. The given function is $y=\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2x+5)-1,$ and to write the inverse function implicitly, we swap $x$ and $y$ as follows:\n\n$$\nx=\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2y+5)-1\n$$\n\nNote that in the equation above, we have $y={g}^{-1}(x).$\n\n**Step 2:** Next, we differentiate. The overall goal is to find $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x},$ but the equation is already solved for $x,$ so we compute $\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}y}$ and then take the reciprocal:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}y} & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}y}(\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2y+5)-1) \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}y} & =\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2y+5)\\cdot 2 \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}y} & =2\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2y+5) \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =\\frac{1}{2\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2y+5)} \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{sec}⁡(2y+5)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n**Step 3:** Lastly, we write the result in terms of ${g}^{-1}(x).$ Since $y={g}^{-1}(x),$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}[{g}^{-1}(x)] & =\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{sec}⁡(2{g}^{-1}(x)+5) \\\\ {({g}^{-1})}^{′}(x) & =\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{sec}⁡(2{g}^{-1}(x)+5).\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186390764 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186179701 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "d8033e21-86ab-5dc6-8060-a0b5c134bf9d" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Regions Where a Function Is Positive or Negative Using a Sign Table"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "dae056ab-7845-5fc5-8a65-cdde9b2cbb30" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "+" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186390766} {:answer/id #uuid "27cd30f8-4c67-5b18-ae74-5d01e606d486" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186390767}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "dae056ab-7845-5fc5-8a65-cdde9b2cbb30" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "+" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186390766} :answer-field/id #uuid "8a74112e-0c08-5638-a489-048657b454f6" :answer-field/key "field-4" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045494 :db/ident :answer-field.type/select} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186390765} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "452c8b52-3ea3-5cb6-9b20-63200080fa73" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "+" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186390769} {:answer/id #uuid "172538d6-798f-5d52-aaa4-e930af45cbbd" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186390770}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "172538d6-798f-5d52-aaa4-e930af45cbbd" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186390770} :answer-field/id #uuid "46fa5dec-49b3-5b2d-90a3-ac28dc1634bb" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045494 :db/ident :answer-field.type/select} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186390768} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "60efd871-1e1b-599a-b039-2a402c71c9a2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "+" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186390772} {:answer/id #uuid "7528b55c-f6ca-5670-a6c9-c97bbcc6a15a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186390773}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "60efd871-1e1b-599a-b039-2a402c71c9a2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "+" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186390772} :answer-field/id #uuid "487b2d06-4c10-5d8f-aa1c-2f69c5ea9f44" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045494 :db/ident :answer-field.type/select} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186390771} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "27855f1e-bf2f-509d-8106-266bf2bf92a0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "+" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186390775} {:answer/id #uuid "c67b32f5-a6af-586c-b222-e36503cdaf3d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186390776}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "c67b32f5-a6af-586c-b222-e36503cdaf3d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186390776} :answer-field/id #uuid "982a0b2e-2dc8-5f75-ad31-7f4aebc78fdb" :answer-field/key "field-3" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045494 :db/ident :answer-field.type/select} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186390774}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "0ff4ec42-4593-525e-b2e1-f274a6430ad8" :question/math-academy-id "q-326436" :question/problem "Consider the function $f(x,y)=-{x}^{3}(y+1).$ Fill in the missing signs in the sign table of $f(x,y)$ shown below.\n\n| $y>-1$ | {{field-1}} | {{field-2}} |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| $y<-1$ | {{field-3}} | {{field-4}} |\n|  | $x<0$ | $x>0$ |" :question/worked-solution "Notice that $f(x,y)$ equals zero when $x=0$ and $y=-1.$ These lines divide the $xy$-plane into four regions, as shown below.\n\n![](images/ec/ecbba4555023bdc89892cd902b30039e3a76a919b68c5a2bec670213dfc78c34.png)\n\nTo determine the sign of $f(x,y)$ in each region, we pick four test points, one for each region.\n\n![](images/9c/9ca3f95ecca25c73eadd7cbd3840cbc1f8336ff7a1a1598876c11bd4af16805b.png)\n\nNext, we calculate the sign of $f(x,y)$ in each region using a sign table:\n\n|  | Test point | $-{x}^{3}$ | $(y+1)$ | $f(x,y)$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| Top-Left | $(-1,0)$ | $+$ | $+$ | $+$ |\n| Top-Right | $(1,0)$ | $-$ | $+$ | $-$ |\n| Bottom-Left | $(-1,-2)$ | $+$ | $-$ | $-$ |\n| Bottom-Right | $(1,-2)$ | $-$ | $-$ | $+$ |\n\n \n\nUsing the *last* column of the table above, we get the following picture:\n\n![](images/e0/e02c333ffb3063ebf0f214cf88cb9a6d486cff0db958de6d47943f3ca0739e45.png)\n\nFinally, we fill in the required sign table.\n\n| $y>-1$ | $+$ | $-$ |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| $y<-1$ | $-$ | $+$ |\n|  | $x<0$ | $x>0$ |"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186120202 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186119939 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "00ac6edc-908a-50be-9ef1-4b24ba597d1d" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating dy/dx Using dx/dy"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "233da062-0046-5ff6-be71-aee3cc7e71f8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{{y}^{3}}{4+4{y}^{4}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186300130} {:answer/id #uuid "95d1ecb0-3160-5adc-97f9-910e8d9c239c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{{y}^{3}}{1+{y}^{4}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186300719} {:answer/id #uuid "b0a94346-e82d-5c11-b3c7-77080761ef66" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{{x}^{3}}{1+{x}^{4}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186300843} {:answer/id #uuid "f6dc110a-2fc4-5a9e-a3d2-5fed13a83b5e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{y}{4+4{y}^{4}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186301179} {:answer/id #uuid "fae0bb00-a872-5722-aa1c-2b78582a5353" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{{y}^{3}}{4+4{y}^{3}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186301204}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "233da062-0046-5ff6-be71-aee3cc7e71f8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{{y}^{3}}{4+4{y}^{4}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186300130} :answer-field/id #uuid "84d7d2bf-ce4d-5963-b71f-6932bfd6b3ea" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186301646}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "cd82fd71-e11f-52b4-879b-d6f659d732bf" :question/math-academy-id "q-32705" :question/problem "If $x=-\\frac{2}{{y}^{2}}+2{y}^{2},$ then $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=$" :question/worked-solution "First, we differentiate $x(y)$ with respect to $y:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}y} & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}y}(-\\frac{2}{{y}^{2}}+2{y}^{2}) \\\\  & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}y}(-2{y}^{-2}+2{y}^{2}) \\\\  & =-2\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}y}({y}^{-2})+2\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}y}({y}^{2}) \\\\  & =4{y}^{-3}+4y \\\\  & =\\frac{4}{{y}^{3}}+4y \\\\  & =\\frac{4+4{y}^{4}}{{y}^{3}}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, taking the reciprocal of $\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}y},$ we get\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}={(\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}y})}^{-1}=\\frac{{y}^{3}}{4+4{y}^{4}}.\n$$"}]}
